thanks:
Thine is the mercy that fostered our grain.
We bring thee our thanks and our garlands for tribute,
The wealth of our valleys, new-garnered and ripe;

thankful:
Good readers of me in some aftertime,
Thankful to some idea of my being
That doth not even my with gone true soul rime;

that'll:
And little the wonder it ripped and tore.
There's one that'll join in their push and roar,
With stories to jabber, and stones to throw;

thaih:
Whippo'will a-tellin' tales
Out thaih in de night;
An' yo' cabin 's 'crost de lot:

An' you sholy got me wrong.
Set down at dat table thaih;
Jes' you whimpah ef you daih!

thawin:
Seen a robin set;
W'y hit 'mence a-thawin',
Groun' is monst'ous wet.

thatch:
Take me far away to the hills that hide your home;
Peace shall thatch the roof and love shall latch the door--
But what if I heard my first love calling me once more?

thalia:
Wandering Heaven and Earth and Hell and the four seasons through;
Thalia, not you,
Not you, Melpomene,
